  "stepTexts": [
   "Pat the 1½ pounds of shrimp dry with paper towels, then toss with ½ tablespoon of the cornstarch and set aside.",
   "Mince the 5 garlic cloves and finely grate 1½ tablespoons of fresh ginger; remove strings from the 8 ounces of snap peas and thinly slice the 2 red bell peppers.",
   "Whisk together 3 tablespoons soy sauce, 2 tablespoons oyster sauce, 1 tablespoon rice vinegar, 1 tablespoon sesame oil, 1 tablespoon cornstarch, ¼ cup chicken stock, and ½ teaspoon crushed red pepper flakes into a smooth sauce.",
   "Heat 1 tablespoon neutral oil in a large wok or skillet over high heat until shimmering, then add the shrimp in a single layer and sear 1½ minutes per side until just pink; transfer to a plate.",
   "Add the remaining 1 tablespoon neutral oil to the wok over high heat, then stir-fry the bell pepper and snap peas for 3 minutes until just tender-crisp.",
   "Push the vegetables to the side, add the garlic and ginger to the center of the wok, and stir-fry for 30 seconds until fragrant.",
   "Pour the sauce into the wok and stir everything together; cook 1–2 minutes until the sauce thickens and coats the vegetables.",
   "Return the shrimp to the wok and toss to coat; cook 30 seconds just to heat through.",
   "Transfer to a serving platter and garnish with the sliced scallions and toasted sesame seeds (optional)."
  ],
