  "stepTexts": [
   "Preheat the oven to 400°F.",
   "Halve the 2 acorn squash lengthwise and scoop out the seeds; brush the cut sides with 2 tablespoons olive oil, season with 1 teaspoon kosher salt and ¼ teaspoon black pepper, then drizzle 1 tablespoon maple syrup evenly over the cut sides.",
   "Rinse 1 cup wild rice blend under cold water.",
   "Finely dice 1 yellow onion and 2 celery stalks, and mince 3 garlic cloves.",
   "Place the squash halves cut-side down on a parchment-lined baking sheet and roast at 400°F for 35–40 minutes until the flesh is tender when pierced with a fork.",
   "While the squash roasts, combine the rinsed wild rice blend with 2 cups vegetable broth and ½ cup water in a medium saucepan; bring to a boil, then reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 40–45 minutes until the grains are tender and the liquid is absorbed.",
   "Melt 2 tablespoons unsalted butter in a large skillet over medium heat; add the onion and celery and sauté, stirring frequently, for 5–6 minutes until softened, then add the garlic and cook 1 minute more.",
   "Remove the skillet from heat and stir in the cooked wild rice, ½ cup dried cranberries, ½ cup roughly chopped toasted pecans, 1 teaspoon fresh thyme leaves, 1 tablespoon finely chopped fresh sage, 1 tablespoon apple cider vinegar, 1 tablespoon maple syrup, ½ teaspoon kosher salt, and ¼ teaspoon black pepper; stir until evenly combined.",
   "Flip the roasted squash halves cut-side up, mound the filling generously into each cavity, and return to the oven for 8–10 minutes until the filling is heated through and the squash edges are lightly caramelized.",
   "Transfer the stuffed squash halves to a platter, scatter 3 ounces crumbled goat cheese over the filling, and garnish with 2 tablespoons chopped fresh flat-leaf parsley; serve immediately."
  ],
